<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<h6 id=3D"Credentials,integrationsandBlockchainFlowcharts-NEEDINSPIRATION?"=
>NEED INSPIRATION?</h6>
<ul>
<li><p>Check out this guide on how to&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://confluence.at=
lassian.com/confcloud/use-confluence-as-a-knowledge-base-724765471.html" cl=
ass=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">use Confluence as a Knowledge base</=
a></p></li>
<li><p>Follow&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://www.atlassian.com/blog/confluence/twi=
tters-5-tips-successful-knowledge-base" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofo=
llow">Twitter's 5 tips for a successful knowledge base</a></p></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"Credentials,integrationsandBlockchainFlowcharts-BlockchainFlowcha=
rts">Blockchain Flowcharts</h1>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;border-color: #998D=
D9;border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;">=20
<p>This space is used to post all the information regarding trials you can =
run. The trials you might need on a regular basis might be transactions mos=
tly but most importantly the behaviour of the network overall and with the =
changes applied through our smart contracts.</p>=20
</div>
</div>
<p><u>The process is the following</u>: </p>
<ol>
<li><p>In order to use the flowcharts you will need test ETH. Get them from=
 the available faucets: <a href=3D"https://faucet.rinkeby.io/" class=3D"ext=
ernal-link" rel=3D"nofollow">Rinkeby</a>, <a href=3D"https://goerli-faucet.=
slock.it/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">G=C3=B6erli</a>, <a hre=
f=3D"https://faucet.ropsten.be/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">R=
opsten</a>, <a href=3D"https://kovan.faucet.enjin.io/" class=3D"external-li=
nk" rel=3D"nofollow">Kovan</a>. </p></li>
<li><p>The platform you will use to visualize such trials is <a href=3D"htt=
ps://eth.build/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">eth-build</a>. Th=
is works as a playgroung where you can prototype constructors, code structu=
res you are building, etc. It is highly recommended to check the <a href=3D=
"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLJz1HruEnenCXH7KW7wBCEBnBLOVkiqIi=
" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">tutorials available</a> on the t=
opic to understand how to use it: </p></li>
</ol>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper"><img =
class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"d5=
5d8d01ad09efdee3c819383683c479" data-image-src=3D"https://creativetoken.atl=
assian.net/wiki/download/attachments/590134/image-20210227-172113.png?versi=
on=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1614446479194&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3D=
v2" data-height=3D"1338" data-width=3D"2418" data-unresolved-comment-count=
